course: dictionary
lesson: 14224
title: Words that keep coming back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nagging can mean three different things. Use the words around it to find the right one. Read the whole sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «Mum kept nagging me to tidy my room.» Here nagging means telling someone again and again, in an annoying way. The word «kept» is your clue: it means it happened over and over.
explain: «Her cough was nagging her all week.» A nagging cough is one that goes on and on and will not go away. «He had a nagging doubt about the answer» means a small worry that keeps coming back.
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of nagging. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one. Nag, nags, nagged and nagging all come from the same verb, nag.
fact: Nagging means telling someone again and again to do something, in an annoying way.
fact: A nagging pain or feeling goes on and on and will not go away.
fact: A nagging doubt or worry is a small worry that keeps coming back.
fact: Nag, nags, nagged and nagging all come from the same verb, nag.
fact: A child might say, «Stop nagging!» when a grown-up keeps asking them to tidy up.
exercise: «My sister kept nagging me to finish my homework.» What does nagging mean here? | Sleeping on the sofa | Helping me with my sums | Singing a happy song | *Telling me again and again in an annoying way
exercise: «I had a nagging headache all afternoon.» What does nagging tell you about the headache? | It made me laugh | It was very loud | It came and went in a second | *It went on and on and would not go away
exercise: Which word shows that the worry keeps coming back? «I had a nagging doubt that I had locked the door.» | door | locked | *nagging | had
test: Which phrase means a small worry that keeps coming back? | *A nagging doubt | A loud bang | A bright light | A sunny day
test: «Dad's nagging about my bedroom has not stopped since Monday.» What does nagging mean here? | Reading a long book quietly | Playing a game with a friend | Painting a picture | *Asking again and again in an annoying way
exam: «The nagging cough kept Ella awake all night, so her mum took her to the doctor.» What does nagging mean here? | A cough from eating sweets | *A cough that goes on and on and will not go away | A cough that is very loud | A cough that stops suddenly
